{
  "id": "22289_nukinderu",
  "headword": "{抜|ぬ}きん{出|で}る",
  "reading": "ぬきんでる",
  "romaji": "nukinderu",
  "part_of_speech": "verb (ichidan)",
  "gloss": "to stand out; to excel; to surpass others",
  "definitions": [
    {
      "sense_number": 1,
      "gloss": "to stand out; to excel; to surpass others",
      "explanation": "To be markedly superior to others in ability, skill, or achievement. A literary and somewhat elevated expression."
    }
  ],
  "examples": [
    {
      "id": "22289_nukinderu_ex1",
      "japanese": "{彼|かれ}の{才能|さいのう}は{抜|ぬ}きん{出|で}ている。",
      "english": "His talent is outstanding.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    },
    {
      "id": "22289_nukinderu_ex2",
      "japanese": "{数学|すうがく}の{成績|せいせき}で{抜|ぬ}きん{出|で}た{存在|そんざい}だ。",
      "english": "He is a standout when it comes to math grades.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    },
    {
      "id": "22289_nukinderu_ex3",
      "japanese": "{多|おお}くの{候補者|こうほしゃ}の{中|なか}から{抜|ぬ}きん{出|で}た{実力|じつりょく}で{選|えら}ばれた。",
      "english": "She was chosen from among many candidates thanks to her outstanding ability.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    }
  ],
  "notes": "A literary verb meaning to rise above the rest. Most often appears in the ている form ({抜|ぬ}きん{出|で}ている) to describe an ongoing state of excellence. Originally from classical Japanese {抜|ぬ}き{出|い}づ.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {才能|さいのう}が{抜|ぬ}きん{出|で}ている: one's talent is outstanding\n- {実力|じつりょく}で{抜|ぬ}きん{出|で}る: to excel through ability\n- {群|ぐん}を{抜|ぬ}いて{抜|ぬ}きん{出|で}る: to stand far above the rest\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- {優|すぐ}れる: to excel — more common and less literary; used in everyday contexts\n- {秀|ひい}でる: to excel — literary, similar register; emphasizes shining brilliance\n- {傑出|けっしゅつ}する: to be outstanding — more formal and written; used for notable figures",
